 "about": "Measured values of an open-access article, in the format of thermoml_<id>.json (read by measured_components.ThermoML together with the ThermoML file). Extracted with pdftotext from the text layer of the article's PDF; vapour pressures converted from Pa to kPa (the unit of the ThermoML property name), pressures of the density table from MPa to kPa. Uncertainties: the expanded (95 %) uncertainties stated in the article. Levoglucosenone (the maintainer, 2026-10-22: data of the article found again; it had been used for cyrene only): Table 19 (vapour pressure, gas saturation method, 298-403 K) and Table 13 (liquid density at 0.100 MPa, 293-363 K; the table lists the seven temperatures twice and 298.15 K a third time, all kept as printed). Purity (Section 2.1): the sample for the vapour pressures was 96.2 wt % (light impurities and 2-methoxyphenol); the first run, with a much higher pressure, was removed by the authors, and the condensate after the measurement was 98.5 wt %; the density sample was distilled to 98.7 wt %.",
